: false, "num_turns": 3, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "I found 11 rules whose behavior didn't match their docstrings and fixed them in `pricebook.py`. After the fixes I ran a check of all 150 rules against what their docstrings say, using a grid of qty/unit values, and none differ.\n\n| Rule | Problem | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| 11 | The cap was applied to the price, so the discount came out as `min(base, 30000) * 5%` | Cap the discount at 30,000 won |\n| 36 | The cap only kicked in when the discount was over 100,000 won | Always cap at 50,000 won |\n| 40 | `qty > 12` | `qty >= 12` |\n| 42 | Marginal rule, but the discount was taken on the whole amount | `(qty - 30) * unit * 12 // 100` |\n| 63 | Used 9% | 8% |\n| 70 | The cap only kicked in when the discount was over 60,000 won | Always cap at 30,000 won |\n| 85 | Used 6% | 5% |\n| 113 | `qty > 100` | `qty >= 100` |\n| 134 | Used 3% | 2% |\n| 137, 140 | `round()` rounded to the nearest won | Floor with `//` |\n\nI also changed rule 82 from `qty >= 51` to `qty >= 50` for consistency. Its prices don't change, because at qty 50 the marginal discount is 0 either way.\n\nSTATUS: DONE", "ttft_ms": 1605, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 20853, "uuid": "5eca79f4-4420-4816-8ded-464b6459052b", "ttft_stream_ms": 922, "time_to_request_ms": 233, "time_to_request_phases_ms": {"other": 8, "system_prompt": 20, "resume_other": 0, "process_user_input": 1, "input_attachments": 3, "input_hooks": 1, "transcript_persist": 12, "tool_pool_refresh": 1, "init_message": 3, "engine_pickup": 1, "message_prep": 0, "model_config_wait": 0, "autocompact": 1, "query_setup": 0, "model_gates": 171, "tool_schema_build": 6, "message_normalization": 1, "client_creation": 2, "request_build": 2}, "turn_start_resume_kind": "none", "process_turn_index": 0, "time_to_request_loop_lag_ms": 1, "time_to_request_cpu_ms": 153, "time_to_request_major_faults": 0, "input_attachments_detail": {"slowest_producer": "model", "slowest_producer_ms